On 9 Aug 2005 I posted my YAFAP, Beren Belagund the Slayer. Today I'm
happy to post YAAP, Minsc the Conqueror! At the time of my first
ascension, I had a couple of other barbarian savegames from a few
months back. This second ascension of mine is a continuation of one of
those, which got stalled a few months ago at the Valley of the Dead, so
I decided over the past week to finish up the game in little bits of
time off and on. Since I used NethackW.exe for this one, I gave up
trying to copy out my main inventory by hand (I was able to
copy-and-paste the rest, however).

Compared with last time, my score was about 700k greater, I used three
fewer wishes, and I geno'ed half the number of species. So it was a bit
of an improvement :-)

At one point near the endgame I accidentally polymorphed myself into a
silver dragon by drinking an unidentified smoky potion. I had to wish
myself up a new cloak of magic resistance. Amazingly enough, I never
had to quaff a single healing potion on any of the elemental planes or
Astral. And I once again picked the correct altar the first time.
Finally, I dumped all my gold and gems before entering the elemental
planes, in order to guarantee unburdened status. Oh well.

Perhaps I'm mistaken, but if you arrive on Astral without conflict, and
then move a bit away from your guardian angel and put on conflict,
hostile angels don't appear. Is this correct? It sure seemed like it.

Also, is it possible to use telepathy to make an *educated* guess about
which is the correct altar? Being neutral, I simply looked for the
altar that had the largest number of priest(esse)s of Crom, and went
for it. Perhaps it was just a coincidence.

I have one more barbarian to finish up, and then it's off to Valkyries,
I think.


